@* ─── Run steps at row height (#1162) ───
   The whole run as a row of segments, one per step, each carrying that step's outcome. The labels,
   icons and durations of the Activity page's rail are all dropped: at this size the only thing a
   segment can say is how the step turned out, and that is enough to see where a run has got to and
   whether anything was skipped or failed.

   Deliberately no tooltips. A segment is a few pixels wide, so eight of them are eight poor hover
   targets; the caption beneath the rail names the step that matters, and the row's name links to
   the Activity, where the labelled rail lives. *@

@if (Steps.Count > 0)
{
    <div class="jim-queue-steps" data-testid="jim-queue-steps">
        @foreach (var step in Steps)
        {
            <span class="jim-queue-step jim-queue-step--@RunPhaseVisuals.StatusModifier(step.Status)"
                  data-testid="jim-queue-step"></span>
        }
    </div>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The run's own steps, in run order. Renders nothing when empty, which covers Worker Tasks
    /// that are not Run Profile executions.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<RunPhaseStep> Steps { get; set; } = [];
}
